WEBVTT

00:22.439 --> 00:25.150
<i>Welcome to the audio commentary
for</i> Rear Window.

00:25.609 --> 00:26.818
<i>I'm John Fawell,</i>

00:26.902 --> 00:29.780
<i>author of</i> Hitchcock's Rear Window:
The Well-Made Film.

00:30.948 --> 00:33.534
<i>This film begins,
as so many Hitchcock films do,</i>

00:33.617 --> 00:35.536
<i>with a camera peering through a window.</i>

00:36.203 --> 00:37.829
<i>Hitchcock loved to shoot through windows,</i>

00:37.913 --> 00:40.624
<i>which, of course,
provide excellent framing devices.</i>

00:41.667 --> 00:43.794
<i>But shooting through windows
also gave Hitchcock the chance</i>

00:43.877 --> 00:47.381
<i>to underline the voyeurism
inherent in watching a film.</i>

00:48.298 --> 00:50.092
<i>The shades being raised in Jeff's windows</i>

00:50.175 --> 00:53.804
<i>remind us of the curtains lifted in a theater
before a performance.</i>

00:54.471 --> 00:55.931
<i>And this is just one of many times in this film</i>

00:56.014 --> 01:00.477
<i>that Hitchcock will draw a parallel
between Jeff's window and the movie screen,</i>

01:00.769 --> 01:04.147
<i>between watching a film
and being a peeping Tom.</i>

01:15.450 --> 01:17.828
<i>So, in just a moment,
we'll see Hitchcock's name,</i>

01:17.911 --> 01:20.872
<i>and it comes with a musical flourish,</i>

01:21.415 --> 01:24.001
<i>at which point the camera
will snap into action,</i>

01:24.334 --> 01:26.503
<i>going through this window and taking a pan,</i>

01:27.170 --> 01:30.882
<i>the first of six counter-clockwise pans
around the courtyard.</i>

01:30.966 --> 01:31.967
<i>Here's the name.</i>

01:34.511 --> 01:36.680
<i>And the flourish, and we start to move.</i>

01:36.763 --> 01:40.434
<i>This is the first of six
counter-clockwise pans</i>

01:40.517 --> 01:43.937
<i>that Hitchcock is gonna repeat,
that operate almost as chapter headings</i>

01:44.021 --> 01:45.856
<i>or little breaks throughout the film.</i>

01:46.815 --> 01:48.692
<i>This cat climbing the stairs introduces us</i>

01:48.775 --> 01:50.277
<i>to the part of the set
that we're gonna see later</i>

01:50.360 --> 01:52.237
<i>when Stella and Lisa jump over that fence.</i>

01:52.321 --> 01:54.781
<i>I think that's why
Hitchcock put it in there, this scene.</i>

01:56.408 --> 01:58.118
<i>This is our introduction to this set.</i>

01:58.201 --> 01:59.453
<i>We're really not looking at the neighbors yet.</i>

01:59.536 --> 02:02.080
<i>This is just Hitchcock giving us
